### **Step 4: Find $ t $ from Equation 1**

From Equation 1:

$$
\frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4
$$

Plug in $ s \approx 2.3166 $:

$$
\frac{9}{2.3166} \approx 3.88 \text{ hours} = 232.8 \text{ minutes}
$$

So:

$$
\frac{t}{60} = 4 - 232.8 = -228.8 \Rightarrow t = -228.8 \times 60 = -13728 \text{ minutes}
$$

This is **not possible** (negative time). So we must have made a mistake.

