### Step 4: Separate real and imaginary parts

Let’s write the complex number as:

$$
z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)
$$

So:

$$
e^{i\theta} = \cos\theta + i\sin\theta
$$
$$
e^{-i\theta} = \cos\theta - i\sin\theta
$$

Now compute:

$$
A = 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)
